How many tokens are produced by a C lexical analyzer for the code below? Comments produce no tokens, a string literal or character constant is one token, and multi-character operators are one token each.

```c
int main() {
  /* count = 0; */
  char *s = "a+b;";  // tail
  return s[0]++ != 'a';
}
```

Consider the syntax-directed definition below. `num.lexval` is the integer value supplied by the scanner.

```
E -> E1 # T    { E.v = E1.v * T.v }
E -> T         { E.v = T.v }
T -> T1 & F    { T.v = T1.v - F.v }
T -> F         { T.v = F.v }
F -> num       { F.v = num.lexval }
```

