A bottom-up (LR) parser uses the translation scheme below. Each action runs when its production is reduced.

```
S -> A B      { print 0 }
A -> a A      { print 1 }
A -> b        { print 2 }
B -> c B      { print 3 }
B -> d        { print 4 }
```

